# roar state — the generated setup stage runs `roar init`, which creates
# .roar/. Without this rule the worktree goes dirty and the FIRST PAID
# `roar run` refuses to execute ("Run blocked: untracked files").
.roar/
# --- reproduction outputs (scaffold_row.py: mnist rule) ---
# file-pattern ignore + tracked .gitkeep so each dir survives a clean
# checkout and roar keeps the outputs in lineage. NEVER dir-ignore.
pretrained/*
!pretrained/.gitkeep
finetune_csv/finetuned/*
!finetune_csv/finetuned/.gitkeep
# NOTE: the final artifact dir
#   finetune_csv/finetuned/<exp_name>/basemodel/best_model/
# is created at runtime by finetune_base_model.py (os.makedirs) and sits BELOW
# an ignored parent, so git cannot re-include a .gitkeep inside it. The two
# rules above are the ones that matter.
